# Every text file is LF in the working tree on every platform. Generated
# files (flatpak/, linux/, snap/) are compared byte for byte against a fresh
# render by cmd/linuxmeta's tests, source-scanning tests match "\n", and the
# toolkit patches apply to LF sources; a CRLF checkout on the Windows runner
# broke all three. Binary files are detected by content.
* text=auto eol=lf
